- "callsign" could be considered as an "alternateIdentifierValue" under the "AlternateIdentifier" (bsm:AlternateIdentifier) class.
- "onground" could influence the type of location or activity but doesn't directly map to a property without more context.
- "squawk" is similar to "callsign" in that it could be another form of identifier.
- "baroaltitude" and "geoaltitude" both relate to the "altitudeMeters" property of the "Altitude" (bsm:Altitude) class.

Given the complexity and the specific nature of the data, the confidence in these mappings can vary, but they are primarily based on the column names and the structural position of the data.

